# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# WHY (2026-07-31): core.autocrlf was unset while the working tree held CRLF
# files, so git reported every CRLF file as entirely rewritten. A commit of
# ~1,000 lines of real changes appeared as 14,310 insertions / 13,573
# deletions — unreviewable, and it would have buried the order-routing fixes
# in noise. `text=auto` stores LF in the repo and leaves the working tree
# alone, so this can't recur on either PC.

* text=auto

# Explicit: source and data are text
*.py    text
*.js    text
*.json  text
*.md    text
*.yml   text
*.yaml  text
*.toml  text
*.csv   text
*.pine  text

# Explicit: never touch binaries
*.parquet binary
*.xlsx    binary
*.docx    binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.ipynb   binary
